00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.710
final

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.710
episode

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:27.750
"Adieu, My Beloved Oscar"

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.240
André...

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.440
Lady Oscar...!

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.830
Commander!

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.000
Commander Oscar!

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.200
Hang in there! Can you hear me?!

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.200
Commander!

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.840
Don't yell, Alain...

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.170
I can hear you...

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.660
What are you all doing?!

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.460
Give me a hand!

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.630
Move her to a safe place!

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.020
Fire!!

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.310
This way! Hurry up!

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.240
Bernard!

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.110
Hold on.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.020
Oscar is...!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.750
Let me down, Alain...

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.530
Let me down...

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.780
Please... I beg you...

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.120
I'm very tired...

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.530
Five minutes is enough...

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.530
I want to rest in peace...

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:47.910
Doctor!

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.370
Spread the blanket.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.430
Doctor...

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.500
Someone please wipe the blood off of her face.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:06.850
I'll do it...

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.050
What's the matter?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.110
I can't hear the sound of our cannons firing.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.460
Fire! Keep firing the cannons...!

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:24.070
Bring down the Bastille...!

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.960
Fire, Alain! Keep firing!

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:26.700
What are you waiting for?!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.000
Former French Guardsmen!

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.660
Everyone, get to your positions!

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.700
Fire... Keep firing...

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.280
All right!

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:53.820
Everyone!

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:54.850
Fire away!

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.830
All right! Charge!

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.090
Can you hear them, Oscar?

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.930
It's the voice of the people
mounting an all-out assault.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.010
Adieu...

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.210
No!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:49.280
July 14, 1789, Oscar François dies! ........ And an hour later ........ Bastille Prison surrenders by waving a white flag........

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:11.710
<i>The revolution did not end with
the people's victory at Bastille.</i>

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:17.230
<i>The revolution, in its true meaning,
was now about to begin.</i>

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:21.600
<i>In other words, establishing a new social system,</i>

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.090
<i>and putting the deposed rulers
on trial by the hands of the victors.</i>

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.990
<i>In fact, it could be said that most of the
bloodshed of the French Revolution...</i>

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:35.470
<i>...took place not during the battles,
but afterwards.</i>

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.060
Hey, Alain!

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:53.260
Squad Leader Alain!

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:54.700
It's me!

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:55.660
Bernard!

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.530
Hey, Bernard!

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.350
It's been awhile!

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:00.470
Awhile is an understatement!

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:01.810
Bastille was 5 years ago!

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.710
Sheesh, 5 years?

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:04.840
Has it really been that long?

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.670
I've been looking for you for a while now.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:10.010
Why did you disappear without saying
a word after the fall of the Bastille?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.820
My mother and little sister's graves are here.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.880
I always planned on becoming a farmer here.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.150
It's the same.

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:26.040
Oscar and André are resting side by side on a
small hilltop in Arras, just like those graves.

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:28.530
Oscar and André, huh...

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.620
In a way, they were fortunate.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.990
They died without knowing the ugliness
that followed after the revolution.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.680
October 1, 1789

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:44.880
Just you watch!

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:46.520
I'll chop that woman's head off myself!

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:50.320
We're starving ourselves,
but that Austrian woman said,

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:53.490
''If they have no bread, let them eat cake!''

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.940
<i>On October 1, 1789,</i>

00:09:56.940 --> 00:10:03.620
<i>the women's anger exploded due to the continuing
food shortage, even after the revolution.</i>

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:07.470
<i>And their anger was solely directed at Antoinette.</i>

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:13.300
<i>The men joined them and a mob of over
6000 people, marched towards Versailles.</i>

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:40.950
You must escape! To a safe pl—

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.210
Where's the Queen?!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.120
Capture her and tear her apart!

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.050
Drag the Queen out!

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:00.510
Drag the Queen out to the balcony!

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.440
Your Majesty, you mustn't!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:11.930
Appearing before them is dangerous!

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:12.530
Your Majesty!

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:13.940
Lady Antoinette!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.650
There she is! Damn sow!

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:20.600
It's all her fault, everyone is...!

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:39.500
<i>The last queen of the Bourbon Dynasty,
which had continued for 200 years...</i>

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:44.720
<i>Marie Antoinette had finally
bowed deeply to the people.</i>

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.190
<i>The people fell silent.</i>

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:50.870
<i>Aside from their conviction in
their victory of the revolution,</i>

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.560
<i>the people were struck...</i>

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:57.410
<i>...by Antoinette's dignity to adamantly remain
as queen, even while bowing her head.</i>

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.720
<i>I won't accept it!</i>

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:07.410
<i>I'll never accept the revolution!</i>

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:15.060
The National Assembly has already stripped
the clergy and nobility of their privileges,

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:19.860
and the Revolutionary Tribunal is holding
trials in Paris, almost every day.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:25.330
Members of the nobility with unfavorable reputations among
the people, are being sentenced to death one after another.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:31.430
So then, how is Her Majesty?

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:31.430
Yes,

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:38.220
the royal family was moved from the Palace of Versailles
to Tuileries Palace, by the demand of the people.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.220
What?!

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:42.280
You mean that old Tuileries Palace where
no one has stepped foot in for 150 years?!

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.920
<i>Well, well. I'm quite content here.</i>

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:48.290
<i>If we clear the dust a bit, I'm sure
it'll be a comfortable home.</i>

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.890
To think that it would come to this...

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:52.960
I pity their plight...

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:55.790
The palace is surrounded by soldiers at all times,

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:59.020
and the royal family has only a few
servants to tend to their needs.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.120
All right!

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.150
I've heard enough.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:02.250
Yes.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.390
Ah, wait.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:05.860
When will we receive more news?

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:11.610
Yes, the next mounted messenger will be dispatched
to Sweden in three days, at most.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.700
Oscar, you may be gone,
but you're still in my heart.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.660
Give me courage!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:26.780
Lend me Pegasus' wings,
that took you to Heaven!!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.040
Lend me your white wings!

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.960
I pity Fersen.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:39.130
It was his passion that ultimately
damned Marie Antoinette.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:47.040
While Madame Polignac and the other nobles
who surrounded the Queen fled the country,

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:49.550
Fersen was the only one who came back to Paris.

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:09.820
I have returned to die with you...

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.590
So I could be your shield and support...

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.290
Fersen...!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:25.210
<i>On June 20, 1791,</i>

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.000
<i>a single carriage left Paris and
slipped away into the night.</i>

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:32.930
<i>Risking everything, it was an escape
plan that Fersen had organized.</i>

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:45.660
Hey! Over here!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:46.560
Over here!

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.440
Your Majesty, we have arrived in Bondy.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.770
We'll rest here for a short
while and switch horses.

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:57.340
Please do not worry.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.700
Now that we are here, the last leg will bring
us straight to Pont-de-Somme-Vesle.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.490
General Bouillé, who has arranged
for your border crossing,

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:04.760
has sent his cavalry and will
be waiting for you there.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:07.710
Count Fersen.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:09.090
Yes?

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:10.690
Thank you for this.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:12.620
Now that we've come this far,
I'm sure we'll be safe.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:15.060
Therefore, I'd like you to go back now.

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:17.720
B-But Your Majesty!

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:19.430
It's best we part here.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:23.690
If something goes awry, I don't want to
put you, a foreigner in harms way.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:31.940
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:36.170
Then, I will flee to Belgium from here.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:38.530
Please be careful.

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:41.700
I'll never forget your friendship.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:44.100
I'm sure the Queen feels the same.

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.910
Well then, please be safe!

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:55.220
I pray that it will be successful!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:11.550
<i>It was an eternal farewell fit for a love that
could never be brought out into the light.</i>

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:16.330
And then their escape failed miserably.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.970
Well, no surprise there.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:24.830
The Queen's ill repute and haughty mug are
well known throughout France, after all.

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.510
After the royal family's identity was
found out in the town of Varennes,

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.800
they were immediately taken back to Paris.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.720
It's the King!

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:32.760
It's Louis XVI!

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:36.220
The King tried to abandon and flee from
his own country! Damn bastard!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.390
Look! That woman is Antoinette!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.720
Drag them out and execute them!

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:40.720
Burn them at the stake!

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.560
Show your damn face!

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:44.160
Show your face!

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:48.470
The trip back to Paris took 3 days.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:53.120
I heard the carriage was surrounded by a mob and
caused a huge ruckus in every town along the way.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.670
<i>The sheer terror of that journey...</i>

00:16:57.670 --> 00:17:00.190
<i>...had made Antoinette's beautiful blonde hair...</i>

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:03.120
<i>...turn white, as though she were an old woman.</i>

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:13.220
<i>The royal family's escape attempt...</i>

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:18.210
<i>...had caused the people to lose what
little respect they had left for them,</i>

00:17:18.210 --> 00:17:22.160
<i>and the people began to openly
demand that they be put on trial.</i>

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:28.280
<i>In August of 1792, the royal family,
who are now to be put on trial,</i>

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.480
<i>was moved from Tuileries Palace to the
Temple Tower in the Marais district.</i>

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:37.430
<i>In September, the National Convention was
established, replacing the National Assembly,</i>

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:40.090
<i>while abolishing the monarchy at the same time.</i>

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:43.160
<i>France had declared to the world
that it would become a republic.</i>

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:50.790
Representative of Picardy province,
Florelle de Saint-Just.

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.560
Sovereignty originally resided with the people!

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:58.010
By monopolizing it, the King had deprived
the people of their rights!

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:03.840
Therefore, the King's own existence
is itself an unforgivable crime!

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.480
The King is the crime!

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:10.980
It gives me the chills knowing
Louis XVI is still alive.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.680
Yeah!

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.320
That's right!

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:17.550
Next, Maximilien de Robespierre!

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.190
Louis XVI is not a defendant!

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:25.910
As we are not God, we do not
have the right to judge!

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.130
However!

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:31.270
We have the right to choose a just
path for the future of our country!

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:32.670
Let me be frank.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:35.600
Louis is a threat to our republic!

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:39.590
His very existence is criminal!

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:41.070
That's right!

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:45.820
<i>361 yeas against 360 nays.</i>

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:49.860
<i>Louis XVI was condemned to death
by a mere one vote margin.</i>

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:54.730
<i>On January 21, 1793, the following year,</i>

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:59.460
<i>Louis XVI perished on the guillotine.</i>

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:03.290
Charles!

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:04.310
Charles!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:05.240
Mother!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:06.740
Let him go!

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:09.250
You took my husband and now my child?!

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:12.580
You have children yourselves, don't you?!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:15.940
You're right.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:17.630
We had sons, as well.

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:24.390
While we had no milk to feed our sons and
helplessly watched them die of malnutrition,

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:29.890
you were eating splendidly, wore jewels
and were laughing in Versailles!

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.460
Now, take him away!

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:34.200
Yes!

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:44.450
Shortly after that, Her Majesty
was also sentenced to death.

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:46.970
Hey, let's drop it.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.660
I couldn't care less about
what happened to the Queen.

00:19:50.380 --> 00:19:54.500
Bernard, did you come all this
way just to tell me all this?

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.200
No, that's not why.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:20:00.130
I came to learn about Oscar and André from you.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:03.860
I'm currently writing a book titled,
''A Brief History of the French Revolution.''

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:06.470
I'd like to mention them in my book.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:09.130
At the very least,
you're someone who knew them both.

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:10.500
Then, even more so!

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.940
A condemned Antoinette
has nothing to do with me.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.810
No, in fact, it does.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:17.940
Listen to Rosalie's story a bit more.

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:25.160
I attended to Her Majesty after she
was moved to Conciergerie Prison.

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:29.660
<i>At first, Her Majesty didn't recognize me, but...</i>

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:35.100
Are you that girl Oscar brought to
the ball and introduced me to?

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:37.560
Yes, I'm Rosalie.

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:40.390
I requested to be your attendant
to offer what little comfort I can.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:44.500
Oscar! Oh, the memories!

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.100
Please tell me about Oscar.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.350
Lady Rosalie, please!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:52.970
<i>After that, I told her stories
about Lady Oscar every day.</i>

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:57.910
<i>When I finished, Her Majesty would always say...</i>

00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:01.540
It soothes my heart when I remember Oscar.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.160
October 16, 1793

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:15.300
12:15PM

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:15.300
Marie Antoinette
\h               was beheaded.....

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:22.870
Her Majesty gave me this on
the morning of her final day.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:29.150
She said she made it using cosmetic papers
from her cell, while remembering Lady Oscar.

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:31.680
She also said...

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:35.270
<i>Lady Rosalie, please dye this rose.</i>

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.400
<i>Dye it with Oscar's favorite color.</i>

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.920
When she said that, I realized...

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:46.120
I had never asked Lady Oscar
what color rose she liked.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.530
I wouldn't know about Oscar, but...

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:51.000
André would probably say...

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:54.000
...he likes white...

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:57.460
Then, I should keep it as is?

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.340
Yeah, that's what I'd do.

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.210
<i>A short time later,</i>

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:09.290
<i>Robespierre and Saint-Just lost out in a power
struggle and were beheaded, as well.</i>

00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:11.720
<i>Another decade or so later,</i>

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:15.990
<i>Fersen, who had returned to his
country after Antoinette's death,</i>

00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:19.800
<i>became a cold-hearted lord
who hated his subjects,</i>

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:23.660
<i>and was brutally murdered by his people.</i>

